<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>NYT &gt; Technology</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/section/technology</link><description>Technology industry news, commentary, and analysis, with reporting on big tech, startups, and internet culture. The New York Times is a hub for conversation about news and ideas.</description><atom:link rel="self" href="https://rss.nytimes.com/services/xml/rss/nyt/Technology.xml" type="application/rss+xml" /><item><title>Google Earth Disables A.I. Tool After One Day Over Disinformation Concerns</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/08/02/technology/google-earth-ai-satellite-images.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/08/02/technology/google-earth-ai-satellite-images.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</guid><atom:link rel="standout" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/08/02/technology/google-earth-ai-satellite-images.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss" /><description>A new Google Earth tool allowed the creation of A.I. deepfake maps. The company quickly pulled it back after users noted there were no safeguards to prevent content that could be harmful.</description><dc:creator>Adeel Hassan</dc:creator><pubDate>Sun, 02 Aug 2026 19:25:56 GMT</pubDate><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Map</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Google Maps</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Artificial intelligence</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Computers and the Internet</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Tech Industry</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Rumors and Misinformation</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespa